        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "If the Agency cannot grant such leave based on lack of funding, the Union may offer to reimburse, within thirty (30) days of receipt of billing, the Agency for required overtime costs (including: salary, benefits, paid leave time, pensions and all other employer-related costs) to allow the designated employee to take Union business leave. The Agency and the Union agree to meet and discuss and clarify if any overtime costs are to be paid by the Union prior to the requested leave. If no agreement is reached the employee's request may be denied.",
            "block_bbox": [
